<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:course xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="TAM 210" href="schedule/2009/spring/TAM/210.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2009" href="schedule/2009.xml">2009</calendarYear><term id="120091" href="schedule/2009/spring.xml">Spring 2009</term><subject id="TAM" href="schedule/2009/spring/TAM.xml">Theoretical and Applied Mechanics</subject></parents><label>Introduction to Statics</label><description>Forces, moments, couples; resultants of force systems; equilibrium analysis and free-body diagrams; analysis of forces acting on members of trusses, frames, etc.; shear-force and bending-moment distributions; Coulomb friction; centroids and center of mass; applications of statics in design. Credit is not given for both TAM 210 and TAM 211. Prerequisite: PHYS 211; credit or concurrent registration in MATH 241. </description><creditHours>2 hours.</creditHours><sections><section id="36205" href="schedule/2009/spring/TAM/210/36205.xml">AD1</section><section id="36206" href="schedule/2009/spring/TAM/210/36206.xml">AD2</section><section id="36207" href="schedule/2009/spring/TAM/210/36207.xml">AD3</section><section id="36208" href="schedule/2009/spring/TAM/210/36208.xml">AD4</section><section id="36209" href="schedule/2009/spring/TAM/210/36209.xml">AD5</section><section id="36210" href="schedule/2009/spring/TAM/210/36210.xml">AD6</section><section id="36211" href="schedule/2009/spring/TAM/210/36211.xml">AD7</section><section id="38775" href="schedule/2009/spring/TAM/210/38775.xml">AD8</section><section id="36212" href="schedule/2009/spring/TAM/210/36212.xml">AE1</section></sections></ns2:course>